  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Nuts are the business: almonds, pistachios and walnuts are about 55% of Chapter 08 exports, and the EU, India, Viet Nam, the UAE and Türkiye buy mostly nuts.",
    "Canada and Mexico are the fresh-fruit markets and charge nothing under USMCA. Canada’s 2025 counter-tariff on U.S. citrus, peaches, watermelons, pecans and frozen berries ended on September 1, 2025.",
    "China is where tariffs bite: about 35% on raw almonds and 50% on in-shell walnuts today, and more if its tariff exclusions lapse on December 31, 2026 or its 24-point suspension on January 10, 2027.",
    "India is the market to watch: the February 2026 U.S.–India framework names tree nuts and fruit for tariff cuts, but no rates or dates are published yet."
  ],
